# Product rules

- Hidden tags = settings names/group keys — not hardcoded AI lists. No `blacklist_tags` / `hide_ai`.
- **Hide content** (blur, not list exclusion): Settings → Tags → Hide content rules (`content_hide_rules`: id, label defaulting to Rule #N, tag_names, optional message; rules list and each rule are collapsible). Media with any of a rule’s tags is blurred on viewer/detail/scrape/related/duplicates until that rule id is in `content_hide_revealed_rule_ids` (persisted unlock). While locked, media detail also hides source URLs and tags. Viewer **Show hidden content** (after Show/Hide hidden tags): generic confirm then any rule messages. Tap blur: if matching locked rules have messages, only those dialogs; otherwise the generic **Show all of the hidden content?** confirm. In **Select** mode (Viewer, Downloaded previously, Add related files), tapping a blurred card selects it and does not open the reveal dialog. Current-page tag chips / sidebar list only tags from non-blurred files on that page (selected filter tags still stay visible). While any tag filter is active, content-hidden files are omitted from the media list (via exclude_tags for locked rule tag names) until their rules are revealed. Settings has **Hide again** per revealed rule and **Hide all content again**.
- Seeded `ai` group is membership/color only.
- Ratings: half-stars `0.5`…`5` (float `ratings.score`).
- Similar files: images/gifs use pHash. Videos sample four frames with ffmpeg and match identical only. Hamming 0–2 (capped by `phash_threshold`) = Identical (merge in Scrape panel and media detail). 3–threshold = Similar for pictures (keep/discard). SHA-256 skips the second file. `scrape_skip_identical` (Settings and the Scrape page, default off) skips a new download in the identical band and copies tags + URL onto the kept row. Hand-mark from media detail links one or more other files by local database id as identical or similar (earliest id stays primary). **Add related files** opens on the database-id form; **Select a file** opens the shared media grid and hides that form until Done selecting. The open file’s tags start selected, with Clear selected, Search groups, and Show hidden tags. Each page is six other files in one row across the picker width. Select marks the chosen files to the open one. Review cards use **Keep all** / **Keep selected** (checkboxes after the button); identical cards also **Merge into selected**.
- Scrape: top **Source** defaults to **Local**. Gallery sites come only from installed adapters (`data/adapters/*/adapter.json`; tracked sample is `adapters/example/` only — other `adapters/*` gitignored; install via Scrape **Install …** / **Load adapters folder…** — not auto-installed on Run). Empty/missing catalog coerces Source to Local. Site sources keep **Scraper** (agent) and filters; **Local** links PC folders/files in place (no copy into `media/`, no tags on import; SHA-256 + pHash; Include subfolders default on; native OS pickers). Chosen folders/files and the recursive flag persist in `session_settings.json` and always show again on Local; **Sync folders** re-scans the saved folders for new media. Permanent delete removes the library row only for linked files; media detail adds **Delete from local folder** to unlink the disk file too. Linked files serve via `GET /media/{id}/file`. multi-URL union (one URL filter accepts a newline- or comma-separated list, or add multiple URL rows); tag `and` / `or` mode; each Tag row has a free-text input (any site tag) plus the shared colored single-select picker (search + group filters) over library tags; date range filter is date+time (`datetime-local` → `from..to` ISO local); date-only sides still mean start/end of day; site mode requires Source + Scraper before Run; exclude tags use the shared collapsible tag search/group-filter picker with adjacent **Add hidden tags** (merges settings hide tags/groups via `expandHiddenTags`); **limit** counts successful downloads only (skips do not) and does not apply when any URL filter is used (all seeded URLs / listing results are attempted); when the gallery has no more unseen posts the scrape stops even if the limit is unmet; listing **sort** is applied on the gallery (expand Filters → Oldest/Latest) before the download quota so asc+limit takes oldest matches; **Downloaded previously** defaults to this session, optional persisted `scrape_downloads_show_all` lists library by `scraped_at`; page size `scrape_downloads_page_size` (multiples of 18); Select lives directly beside Search tags and remains visible (disabled only with no items); bulk bar can **Add tags** to the selection (same on the Viewer Select bar). Scrape pages open through `scrape_browser` (`auto`|`obscura`|`playwright`): Auto uses Obscura when that binary is installed, otherwise Playwright Chromium. Browsers are scrape-only: while `hide_scrape_page` is on they are never checked, downloaded or updated, Settings hides the Scrape browser panel, and media detail hides Rescrape / Update tags from URLs. With the Scrape page on, missing browsers are offered (Scrape page notice + Settings Download), never auto-installed; installed ones get a launcher update check at most once a day when **Check for updates on start** is on (off by default on a metered connection).
- Viewer tag layout (`viewer_tag_layout`): `chips` (default, filter above the grid) or `sidebar` (left column of current-page tags, 10 per group, stored `usage_count`, click toggles filter; sidebar fills viewport height with docked pagination). Tag names decode HTML entities on display; scrape `normalize_tag_name` uses `html.unescape` so new rows store real characters (e.g. `'` not `&#039;`). Settings groups: **General** (Theme, Display), **Tags** (aliases, hidden tags, Hide content blur rules, Recalculate tag counts, tags per page options), **Viewer** (UI + viewer options including items per page options), **Other** (scrape and tag-order options).
- Viewer full page: column count prefers even rows for the current `pageSize` (so a short last page keeps the same card size with empty trailing cells); may add columns to shrink cards slightly and avoid a leftover viewport scroll. Pagination stays docked at the bottom of the viewer. Dropdown option lists are settings `viewer_page_sizes` (Viewer panel, default 12–96 step 12, range 1–200) and `tags_page_sizes` (Tags → Tags panel, default 25/50/100, range 1–500); Tags always appends **All** (`0`). Default selected Viewer size is `36`. List editors open via **Edit** (summary line beside the button); Save/Cancel/Esc; dirty Cancel/Esc confirms discard. Adding a size inserts in sorted order. Live page size, hide-hidden-tags and **Show discarded** still patch from each page. Removing a size clamps the saved selection to a remaining option. Media grids (viewer, Downloaded previously, Add related files) share **AND** / **OR** for selected tags (`tag_mode`, default AND). Search tags looks up the full library tag list, so a match can be chosen even when that tag is not on the current page; the list then shows files for those tags. A group filter with an empty tag search stays on tags from the current page. **Include all tags** on the group panel then lists every library tag in the selected groups.
- Untyped site tags → `tags_untyped_group` (`default`|`unknown`).
- Media detail tags: first 25 + dark **Show more (+N)** / **Show less** chips; `media_detail_tags_collapsed` default true; session remembers toggle.
- Tag select display (`tags_select_display_mode`): `highlight` | `front` | `panel` (default) — viewer filter + pickers; click chip to toggle (no ×). Tag pickers share collapsible search, match mode and group filters; each surface may add adjacent toolbar actions.
- Launch: detached `pythonw` via `Run.bat` (plain start) or `Run.bat restart` (kill then start; in-app Reload). Tracked `VERSION` (starts at `0.1`) vs local `data/installed_version`: mismatch (or missing stamp) stops a running app, forces pip + frontend rebuild + exe ensure, stamps the version, then starts; match keeps light ensures and, if healthy on port 8000, only opens the viewer. Same gate for `Run.bat` and `Scrap Download.exe`. Bump `VERSION` when recipients should rebuild after `git pull`. The first `Run.bat` dependency install writes `Scrap Download.exe` in the project folder (file description **Scrap Download**). That exe and Run do not restart a running app when versions match: if it is already up they only open the viewer (same as the tray **Open viewer** item) and do not add a second tray icon. Settings **Launch on startup** writes a Startup-folder shortcut to that exe (so Task Manager does not list `pythonw`) and removes the old Run-key entry. **Start minimized** (default on — tray/server only until Open viewer); **display_mode** `window` opens a native WebView2 shell (normal Windows title bar, no browser chrome) via `pywebview`, with Chrome/Edge `--app=` only as fallback; `browser` opens a normal tab; detail fullscreen control; **Media number** = source|db. **`Run.bat restart`** and in-app **Reload** write `data/.skip_open_viewer` (2‑minute TTL), set `SCRAP_SKIP_OPEN_VIEWER`, and pass `--no-open-viewer` so relaunch does not open a second viewer (including the "already running" race, and including a version-triggered restart during Reload). A normal **`Run.bat`** clears a stale skip flag so Run-while-running still opens the viewer. Reload runs `Run.bat restart` and reloads the tab only after `/api/health` reports a new `boot_id` (not the dying process).
- Outside apps and libraries (binaries, extra packages, tools not already installed with the venv) get install and update logic in the launcher (`Run.bat` / `launcher.py`). Do not assume they are already on PATH. Anything used only for scraping stays behind the Scrape page: while `hide_scrape_page` is on, do not probe, download, or update it, and do not show its settings or actions. Same pattern as scrape browsers — offer Download when the Scrape page is on, never auto-install a missing scrape-only tool, and refuse those routes with `require_scrape_page`. Tools the library uses with the Scrape page hidden (ffmpeg frame hashes) are not behind that gate, but they still need launch install logic.
- Important settings keys live in `app_settings` / `types/appSettings.ts` — keep them aligned.
